+Search (plan §2 #127): one `searching.ts` `createSearching` per window store (`store.ts` `search` + `liveResults` from `mergeSearch.ts`, `rangeStore.ts` `search` from `rangeSearch.ts`), the only writer of the query, case, filters and closed groups; the runner in `searchRun.ts` writes only `results` and `running` (full runs by generation, each with its own `Working` matcher, ranks and results, 8 ms slices, one-file re-runs by `changed` after `SEARCH_PAUSE_MS`, stale replies dropped per path; `onFullRun` lets `searching.ts` open every group and count `fullRuns`, one per new search). The merge source's `loadFile` replies go through `landed` with the stop they were sent in (`currentStop`). Matching and rows are `search/`'s only. `SideColumn.vue` holds the left column's width and handle (`usePanelWidth`, "File list width"), its visibility and the islands' overlap between the shown panel and list, with `SearchPanel.vue` (box, Match Case, pane toggles from `searchIcons.ts`, summary words in `searchText.ts`, `SearchResults.vue`'s virtual list, `overflow-x-hidden`: WebKitGTK's overlay scrollbar would take the clicks on the last row, #1719; its keys in `searchListKeys.ts` `stepSearchList`) above `FileList.vue`; both roots call `search.toggleKey` after `fileListKey` (`windowKey`, the one guard). `SearchResults.vue` alone owns the list's scroll position and its active row: each new search (`fullRuns`) scrolls to the top and clears the active row, so Down from the box starts at the first row; rows that shrink below the scroll position clamp it to the end; `keepInView` follows the keys. Hiding the panel while the keyboard is in it or on `<body>`: with a file on screen (both roots pass `SearchPanel` the shown path only while `screen.kind === 'files'`), the pane focused at show — CodeMirror's content element, `role=textbox aria-multiline` — when still connected and the same path is shown, else `focusShownFile`; with no file on screen (Settings, a server log), the element focused at show when still connected, never a go-to. A row asks `goTo` and opens its file; the shown view takes it through `took`. `opening.ts` holds the merge store's file opening (`open`, `pick`, `thenMoveOn`).
